{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-14T16:53:28.191Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"dec610b5c29dc08047ecfcc1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1726","claim:pm-gh1727","claim:pm-gh1728","claim:pm-gh1729","lineage:pm-gh1729","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1726+pm-gh1727+pm-gh1728+pm-gh1729","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1726","claim:pm-gh1727","claim:pm-gh1728","claim:pm-gh1729","lineage:pm-gh1729","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-g2zzus"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A repeatable boolean extension switch mixed in attached and bare forms (--many=false --many) loses its bare occurrences, because Commander never sees the attached form"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found 2026-11-14 while fixing pm-gh1726 on the built CLI. A flag declared value_type boolean with repeatable: true is a switch (value_arity none), so Commander registers it without a value placeholder: a bare --many reaches the list accumulator, while --many=false is unknown to Commander and is read only by the loose parser from command.args. coerceAccumulatedLooseOption in src/sdk/extension/command-options.ts orders values from the loose occurrences whenever any exist, so the Commander-held bare values are dropped: pm <cmd> --many=false --many delivers [false] instead of [false, true], and --many --many=false delivers [false] instead of [true, false]. All-bare (--many --many, fixed in the same PR to [true, true]) and all-attached forms are unaffected. Fix direction: derive list-switch occurrences in argv order from the captured COMMAND_OPTION_TOKENS with the existing scanArgvScope grammar (refuseConflictingArgvOptionSpellings already resolves each spelling with Commander semantics), instead of mixing Commander's accumulator with the loose occurrence list. Duplicate check: searched repeatable boolean switch attached value order argv; pm-wlxf8f (closed) owns scalar spelling conflicts, pm-853a (closed) value-arity predicates; nothing owns list-switch occurrence order."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["argv","cli","extensions","flags"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-14T16:53:28.191Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-14T16:53:28.191Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"pm <cmd> --many=false --many delivers [false, true] and --many --many=false delivers [true, false] on the built CLI; Occurrence order for list switches comes from the same argv scanner that resolves spelling conflicts, so a token consumed as another option's value is never counted; An in-process spec drives mixed, bare-only and attached-only forms, with a negative control showing the pre-fix loss"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ugqx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Every occurrence of a repeatable switch reaches the handler in argv order"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Bare occurrences are dropped when any attached occurrence is present"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1726","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-14T16:53:28.191Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-wlxf8f","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-14T16:53:28.191Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"abe63064bf9cab0a65e64d108061d87dfef6d9871296e62f54b394e1a0b151c9","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b1c74da9e29ba0ffa5202cd82c62341edb79e269628a07972f3c7dbe5a6ef3fa"}
