{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T08:47:02.325Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3s4jwl","claim:pm-8patuh","claim:pm-g2zzus","claim:pm-gh1769","claim:pm-lulgxc","lineage:pm-3s4jwl","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-3s4jwl+pm-8patuh+pm-g2zzus+pm-gh1769+pm-lulgxc","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-3s4jwl","claim:pm-8patuh","claim:pm-g2zzus","claim:pm-gh1769","claim:pm-lulgxc","lineage:pm-3s4jwl","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T08:47:02.325Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implementation evidence (2026-11-23). orderArgvRepeatableSwitchOccurrences (src/sdk/extension/command-options.ts) re-derives the occurrences of every declared repeatable value-less boolean switch from the captured COMMAND_OPTION_TOKENS with the same scanArgvScope walk that refuseConflictingArgvOptionSpellings uses. resolveArgvSpelling gained a tracks selector (scalar flags for the conflict check, repeatable switches for order), and the occurrence sink now receives whether a value was attached with '=', so an attached --many=bogus is still judged as an explicit value by refuseMalformedAttachedSwitchValues while a bare occurrence stays presence. extractCommandScopedOptions (src/cli/runtime/invocation-options.ts) passes the reordered source to the shared coercer; collectCommandOptionScopes is now shared by both callers.\n\nBuilt-CLI cases added to the gh1726 spec: --many=false --many is [false, true], --many --many=false is [true, false], --many --many=false --many is [true, false, true], --many=true --many=false is [true, false], and --many --from-tracker --many=false is [true] because --from-tracker consumes the token after it. Negative control: with the reordering disabled the first mixed case fails with 'expected [ false ] to deeply equal [ false, true ]'. Unit spec covers short alias, ancestor scope, --no-many, the unchanged-source paths and the unordered coercer result beside each ordered one.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T08:47:02.325Z"}],"before_hash":"842f619b0fc50af5ff6da4294f66a4c8840274b198e7882d32c12f4f436175e9","after_hash":"4781ff2154ee1e6f073bdbb4aff06060b83e2647d494ce86982c8014757812ca","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"70b577cc764bddce12aee4957f389d06da9c94f74da84d7e37a877110e09f981"}
