{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T10:16:01.263Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-5mstyv","lineage:pm-5mstyv","lineage:pm-92if","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-5mstyv","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-5mstyv","lineage:pm-5mstyv","lineage:pm-92if","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T10:16:01.262Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 1 on PR #1772 (Codex, 2026-11-23). Fixed: (1) the replacement dropped every loose occurrence under the switch's alias keys, so with -S aliasing --many beside an independent strict --s, --many --s=invalid lost the s occurrence and its strict refusal; replacement now uses the coercer's own key ownership (a key that is another declaration's canonical key stays with it). (2) The loose parser folds --Many=false onto many while the scan looked spellings up verbatim, so the folded value was dropped and --many --Many=invalid escaped strict validation; the scan now folds an unregistered leaf spelling with the loose parser's key normalization. command-options.spec.ts covers both. Deferred: the same switch registered on a command and its subcommand is merged in scope order, not argv order, when the parent consumes a bare occurrence; filed as pm-302reu with the alignment approach.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T10:16:01.263Z"}],"before_hash":"ca09effa21124d3643d322babb56f2ddab2aa471eb1d7f25d4164291e2ddbc34","after_hash":"f62dd1aeb08d78b69774dabf9d71942e41d9e0b9f17bf913ba21c266ea4bebb7","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"953e30d5562002957b9946a797830c3de553e1e3213722ad0aa928c98a33a5e6"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T10:55:36.638Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-5mstyv","lineage:pm-5mstyv","lineage:pm-92if","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-5mstyv","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-5mstyv","lineage:pm-5mstyv","lineage:pm-92if","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T10:55:36.637Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 2 on PR #1772 (Codex, Greptile, CodeRabbit, 2026-11-23). (1) Codex: the scan re-derived loose values from raw argv adjacency, so --many --Many --source x false read --Many as bare true while the loose parser, reading the tokens Commander leaves (--Many false), recorded false. The scan now only reports, in argv order, Commander's own occurrences and the slots of loose occurrences; every loose occurrence keeps the loose parser's value and attached mark. When the scan and the loose parser disagree on the number of loose occurrences, every value is kept, loose ones first. (2) Greptile and CodeRabbit: the folded-spelling fallback read a registered short group -mm as the long --mm before Commander's short-group split; folding now applies to long -- spellings only. Negative control: without the guard the -mm --many=false case delivers [false] instead of [true, true, false]. command-options.spec.ts covers both.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T10:55:36.638Z"}],"before_hash":"f62dd1aeb08d78b69774dabf9d71942e41d9e0b9f17bf913ba21c266ea4bebb7","after_hash":"969620eed2410f6cb17b2b2ae35325936566c682f38a9025ee38257050c52e75","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"973d058832e4b0875a51b66815805eada44a1d2926bc1a7f734e69f4ab2ee5f0"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T11:57:27.931Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T11:57:27.925Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 3 on PR #1772 (CodeRabbit, 2026-11-23). A single-dash spelling that no registered short option owns (-many=false with --many declared without -m) is unknown to Commander and parsed by the loose parser as many=false; the long-only folding guard from round 2 skipped its slot, so the count mismatch fell back to loose-first order. Folding now skips a single-dash token only when its first letter is a registered short option (the -mm short-group case), so -many=false keeps its argv place. The --many/--no-many negation case raised by Codex pass 3 is recorded on pm-302reu.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T11:57:27.931Z"}],"before_hash":"969620eed2410f6cb17b2b2ae35325936566c682f38a9025ee38257050c52e75","after_hash":"45964e5686677c8c9a5fc8ba2230c963bf3dde1a54b65584c6e455bcbb369025","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ed13ea69fad5b3a660c5c4418b41b7dc702ca9695ea2bdabe1fa3213934dea6b"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T13:57:16.177Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/5","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T13:57:16.177Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 6 on PR #1772 (Codex pass 6, 2026-11-23). Regression fixed: a preflight override that rewrites a repeatable switch given only in bare form was ignored, because the reordering re-read the captured argv whenever Commander consumed an occurrence. A switch with no loose occurrence now keeps Commander's accumulated value, which is complete and ordered on its own and is the value an override may have rewritten; only mixed bare and attached forms (the case this item fixes) are reordered. command-options.spec.ts covers the bare-only override and the count-mismatch fallback. The cross-scope order case raised again in this pass stays on pm-302reu.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T13:57:16.177Z"}],"before_hash":"45964e5686677c8c9a5fc8ba2230c963bf3dde1a54b65584c6e455bcbb369025","after_hash":"8045ae73f4bc83af8825c9ca730e64430cd274f4f976926f6b7af7c018bd815d","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"389179cfcfd99f2e890159ec3e18c725e5dbfd769327b8c5a828f55b8d3a4539"}
